SUMMARY (this summary has no legal value — only the full license text,
linked above, is legally binding):

The AGPLv3 is a strong copyleft license. In short, it means:

  - You are free to use, study, modify, and redistribute this software,
    for any purpose, including commercially.
  - If you distribute a modified version, you must release its source
    code under the same license (AGPLv3).
  - If you run a modified version of this software on a server and let
    other people interact with it over a network (e.g. as a web app,
    which is exactly what MyTransition is), you must make the
    corresponding source code available to those users. This is the
    key difference from the plain GPL: network use counts as
    distribution.
  - You must keep copyright and license notices intact, and document
    significant changes you make.
  - The software comes with NO WARRANTY of any kind.

Full legal text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html
